{
  "_comment": "The walkable world. Maps live in data/maps/<id>.json and share this tile legend. 'atlas' is a tile's cell in the town.tiles texture (16x16 tiles); when that texture is missing, placeholder tiles are generated in those cells from 'color' and 'pattern'. 'player' is where a new story starts. fade_time is the map-change fade in seconds (also used when a conversation changes who is where). pace_step_time / pace_wait: seconds per step and the pause at each point for pacing NPCs (an NPC can override them with its own keys). time_of_day: the story's times and where a new story starts; only story events (a dialogue line's 'then' step with 'set_time') change it. card_fade_time: seconds the screen takes to fade out (and back in) around a card. card_time: seconds a transition card ('then': {'card': ...}) stays up (a tap skips it). object_fade_time: seconds a 'fade_out' / 'fade_in' of a world object takes. lighting_presets: one look per time of day; each map names one with 'lighting' (see scripts/core/lighting.gd for every key). A tile's 'glow' names the light/pane kind a preset draws on it.",
  "tile_size": 16,
  "zoom": 2.5,
  "step_time": 0.16,
  "text_speed": 45,
  "fade_time": 0.35,
  "pace_step_time": 0.45,
  "pace_wait": 1.2,
  "card_time": 1.8,
  "card_fade_time": 0.6,
  "object_fade_time": 1.4,

  "time_of_day": { "start": "day", "values": ["day", "night"] },

  "player": { "character": "agador", "map": "town", "cell": [6, 15], "facing": "up" },

